<!-- Geometry pass — the three cards are the three stages of a build (declare · measure · bake). Each
     card is **one shape** (backdrop mode): when a `<shape>` holds a `<col>`, the shape becomes the
     background, and the header, picture, description and label are laid out inside it.

     This slide is the README's "same slide, different themes" sample, so the cards and the frame
     below **write no fill** — the values of `variant="card"` and `card-backdrop` come from the theme.
     Swap the theme and you get a white card with a border (minimal), a white card floating on a grey
     background (harbor), or a one-step-lighter card on navy (aurora). The source is the same. Only
     the header writes `fill="accent1"`: its text is `bg`, so the strip must be an accent in every
     theme, and the built-in themes' `card-header` sets no fill (the color is that theme's accent1).

     Each card puts one piece of evidence for its stage in the middle: the SOML the author writes
     (highlighted with `lang="soml"`), the boxes the browser measured (two dashed borders and their
     four values), and the EMU written into the PPTX (`lang="xml"`). Card heights are not written as
     numbers — the grid takes the remaining height with `grow="1"` and the three cards receive it
     through the grid's stretch. -->
<slide id="geometry" enter="rise">
  <text variant="kicker">Geometry pass</text>
  <h1>The browser computes the coordinates</h1>
  <grid cols="3" gap="lg" grow="1">
    <shape variant="card" type="rounded-rect" w="fill" pad="md">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="between">
        <col gap="sm">
          <shape variant="card-header" type="rounded-rect" fill="accent1" w="fill" h="44" pad="xs">
            <text color="bg" align="center" anchor="center"><strong>① Declare</strong></text>
          </shape>
          <shape type="rounded-rect" fill="alpha(fg, 0.05)" border="none" radius="sm" w="fill" h="104" pad="xs sm">
            <pre lang="soml" size="14">&lt;row gap="md"&gt;
  &lt;shape w="fill"/&gt;
  &lt;shape w="fill"/&gt;
&lt;/row&gt;</pre>
          </shape>
          <p size="20">Authors declare layout with flex and grid. Coordinates have no place in it.</p>
        </col>
        <text role="code" size="16" color="muted">row · col · grid · stack</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
    <shape variant="card" type="rounded-rect" w="fill" pad="md">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="between">
        <col gap="sm">
          <shape variant="card-header" type="rounded-rect" fill="accent1" w="fill" h="44" pad="xs">
            <text color="bg" align="center" anchor="center"><strong>② Measure</strong></text>
          </shape>
          <row gap="sm" w="fill" h="104">
            <shape type="rect" fill="alpha(accent1, 0.12)" border="2 dashed accent1" w="fill" h="fill">
              <text role="code" size="15" color="accent1" align="center" anchor="center">x · y · w · h</text>
            </shape>
            <shape type="rect" fill="alpha(accent1, 0.12)" border="2 dashed accent1" w="fill" h="fill">
              <text role="code" size="15" color="accent1" align="center" anchor="center">x · y · w · h</text>
            </shape>
          </row>
          <p size="20">Headless Chromium measures every element's box. The pass reads only rects.</p>
        </col>
        <text role="code" size="16" color="muted">getBoundingClientRect</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
    <shape variant="card" type="rounded-rect" w="fill" pad="md">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="between">
        <col gap="sm">
          <shape variant="card-header" type="rounded-rect" fill="accent1" w="fill" h="44" pad="xs">
            <text color="bg" align="center" anchor="center"><strong>③ Bake</strong></text>
          </shape>
          <shape type="rounded-rect" fill="alpha(fg, 0.05)" border="none" radius="sm" w="fill" h="104" pad="xs sm">
            <pre lang="xml" size="14">&lt;a:off x="609600"
       y="1714500"/&gt;
&lt;a:ext cx="1562100"
       cy="1066800"/&gt;</pre>
          </shape>
          <p size="20">Measured rects are the PPTX coordinates. 1px = 9525 EMU, converted once.</p>
        </col>
        <text role="code" size="16" color="muted">a:off · a:ext</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
  </grid>
  <shape variant="card-backdrop" type="rounded-rect" w="fill" pad="sm md">
    <text role="caption" align="center">The pipeline speaks logical stage px (16:9 is 1280×720). EMU and pt exist only inside the PPTX renderer.</text>
  </shape>
  <note>This is the second insight — borrow the browser as the layout engine.</note>
</slide>
